Hi all,

I am having the problem previously described on this list by Michaela
Guendel on 25 Oct 2008, but to my knowledge unresolved.
When using the new REngine-based java client with JRI instead of Rserve, I
am having my jvm crash with EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION error. I enclosed a
short example file intended to reproduce this error. Additional details:

- The JRI examples compile and run fine
- The JRIEngine example compiles with one small correction (a call to
close()), but otherwise runs fine too.
- I have not observed this error with JRI alone, only with JRIEngine: I
tried the problematic eval call to HoltWinters() hardcoded in one of JRI
tests and using a TestConsole - both ways no error.
- Following Simon's suggestions, I am not doing any fancy setup, just
setting up R_HOME, adding jri.dll to java library path and adding the needed
jars.

Any help on this will be greatly appreciated. Below is a sample code that
produces an error.
Please let me know if anyone has dealt with this problem before.

Anya
==================================================================

import org.rosuda.REngine.REngine;
import org.rosuda.REngine.JRI.JRIEngine;

public class MyRtest {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            REngine eng =
REngine.engineForClass("org.rosuda.REngine.JRI.JRIEngine");
            System.out.println("R Version: " +
eng.parseAndEval("R.version.string").asString());

            // This generates EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION:
            eng.parseAndEval("HoltWinters(co2)");


            // Had to cast eng to specific implementation in order to
compile,
            // because close() method was commented out in REngine.java (by
mistake?)
            ((JRIEngine)eng).close();
            System.out.println("Done.");

        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}

