Hi Simon,

could you please check whether theres a bug with the NA encoding in 
REngine's RLogical.
I am using R 2.9.1 with a recent rJava / JRI and a current svn version 
of REngine / JRIEngine.

Minimal example:

REngine re = new JRIEngine();
REXPLogical rexp = (REXPLogical) re.parseAndEval("c(TRUE, FALSE, NA, 
TRUE, NA)");

byte[] xs = rexp.asBytes();
for (int i=0; i<xs.length; i++) System.out.println(xs[i]);

/* returns
1
0
2
1
2
I think the internal coding for NA is supposed to be -128 (judging from 
the src) not 2
*/

boolean[] ys = rexp.isNA();
for (int i=0; i<ys.length; i++) System.out.println(ys[i]);

/* returns wrongly
false
false
false
false
false
*/

System.out.println(REXPLogical.isNA(xs[2]));
// also wrong: false

Regards,

Bernd

